<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Vyner Brooke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vyner Brooke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Vyner Brooke was the third and last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-of-sarawak">White Rajah</a> of Sarawak, ruling from 1917. In 1941 he granted a constitution limiting his powers, shortly before the Japanese occupation. In 1946 he ceded Sarawak to the British crown despite strong local opposition, creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown Colony</a> of Sarawak.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-vyner-brooke.jpg" alt="Charles Vyner Brooke" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bassano Ltd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlesvynerbrooke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
